## AgentForge Lean Routing

Use the `lean-routing` skill for engineering tasks where cost-aware delegation applies.

- Run one trivial deterministic operation directly instead of spawning an agent.
- Delegate repetitive/read-heavy/high-volume low-judgment work to `cheap-ops`.
- Delegate tiny exact edits to `cheap-edit`.
- Delegate small pattern-following implementation to `cheap-coder`.
- Use `reviewer` or the parent for meaningful judgment.
- Keep architecture, ambiguity, security, migrations, concurrency, and cross-cutting decisions in the parent.
- Cheap workers return `ESCALATE` rather than guess.
- Verify deterministically whenever possible.
<!-- agentforge:lean-routing:end -->
